<h1><span lang="EN-US">Inspection Mode</span></h1>
<hr align="center" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Inspection capabilities in KUBE allow user to make a visual comparison between a particular scanned surface and a CAD model (or other scanned surface) or to a datum entity. User can compare all data types (except datums)  scan data, meshes, point clouds, polylines, and probe points. Before starting with the inspection both surfaces must be properly registered or there must be a proper transformation active for scanning.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">When finished, the results of this comparison can be saved in:</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">The same</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>sab2</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">file, where the compared entities and inspection settings are saved.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Report in common file formats (</span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>HTML</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">and</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>PDF</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">).</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span lang="EN-US">The results of the inspection can be preview again in a different session of KUBE.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Three inspection commands can be selected from the 3D Inspection menu:</span></p>
<p><img src="../images/3DInspection_menu.gif" width="143px" height="84px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:normal;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:normal;"><a href="References/3D_Comparison.htm" style="font-weight:normal;">Comparison</a></span></b> - Used for online inspection of surfaces as well as for previously scanned (and eventually processed) surfaces. Creates new inspection session.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB"><a href="References/Comparison_Template.htm">Use Last Settings</a> - e</span><span lang="EN-GB">nters in existing inspection session with the same reference and new entity to inspect.</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB"><a href="References/Last_Comparison.htm">Last Comparison</a> - l</span><span lang="EN-GB">oads the last saved inspection session.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">The three comparison types lead to the same inspection mode with same interface and functionality. The only difference between them is the input data and the presence of former inspection session in the current document.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">In</span> <span class="Mode" style="font-weight:bold; text-decoration:none;"><b>Inspection</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">mode you can:</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Make visual settings for the error map.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US">Create and customize</span> label<span lang="EN-US">s.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US">Create 2D sections.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Access useful functions as displaying and visualising statistical information.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US">Generate</span> report<span lang="EN-US">s.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span lang="EN-US">Entering</span> <span class="Mode" style="font-weight:bold; text-decoration:none;"><b>Inspection</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">mode follows one of the three scenarios:</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Select data + reference &gt;&gt; <span style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Inspection</u></span> mode: data inspected.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">No data + reference &gt;&gt; <span style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Inspection</u></span> mode: only reference is displayed &gt; scan new data &gt; data inspected.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Select data + reference &gt;&gt; <span style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Inspection</u></span> mode: data inspected &gt; scan new data &gt; new data inspected and displayed together with the previous inspected data.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="bullet">The second and the third scenarios involve online inspection.</p>
<p><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>See</b></span> <a href="Instant_Inspection.htm">Instant Inspection</a> for details.</p>

